[hangs seen and fixed on the way (MEASURED, each localised by per-layer dispatch)]
  - stream with more than four pending tasks on one shim DMA channel: layer 20 (/model.7/conv/Conv, 16 input chunks per tile) timed out; fixed by a per-channel limit of 4 pending tasks
  - stream with weight packets of a round streamed as one task plus paired output drains and batched awaits: timed out at the whole stream; the emitter awaited a weight task before all activation fills it serves were issued; both experiments are switched off by default and remain to be bisected
  - after two timed-out dispatches the device refused every new hardware context (0xc01e0009; xrt-smi validate -r latency fails the same way, xrt-smi shows no contexts) until a device restart, which needs an elevated shell

